Under certain condition, truncated result may be raised from  the
kernel against and operation on socket.  This occurs if there are
too many database entries in the kernel and socket buffer for the
socket  is insufficient.  If you manipulate many IPsec key/policy
database entries, increase the size of socket buffer or  use  in‐
terface.   Certain  legacy authentication algorithms are not sup‐
ported because of issues with the subsystem.
